      "committer": {
        "name": "jnsagai",
        "email": "jnsagai@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-06T16:48:06Z"
      },
      "message": "Port ThreadX zonal lighting controller to MXChip AZ3166 with UART-CAN\n\nRun the zonal brake/reverse lighting controller on a physical MXChip\nAZ3166 (STM32F412, ThreadX cortex_m4/gnu at the pinned revision) and\nexchange CAN frames with X-Verse over the ST-LINK USB UART using the\nLawicell SLCAN protocol. The unchanged Zenoh2CAN bridge reaches the board\nthrough python-can's slcan interface; the shared lights_protocol.c keeps\nthe 0x1F1/0x1F4 contract identical to the Linux controller.\n\n- Register-level board layer: HSI 96 MHz clock, USART6 IRQ RX and TX\n  ring, LED lamps, SSD1306 OLED status over I2C\n- ThreadX ingress/control/display threads, 1 s heartbeat (0x1F5 diag),\n  lamps off when the SLCAN channel closes\n- SLCAN codec with host unit test, hardware smoke test, flash script\n- configure_bridge.py gains --bus-type/--bitrate (defaults unchanged)\n- Hardware evidence: 11/11 checks passed incl. Zenoh bridge round trip\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
