      "message": "Add live X-Verse/CARLA qualification and ASPICE SWE evidence for AZ3166\n\nLive integration: drive the full run_autoverse.py X-Verse stack through\nVehicle Manual Control keys (XTEST, focus-guarded) and verify the chain\nVCU -> Zenoh2CAN (slcan) -> AZ3166/ThreadX -> virtual vehicle -> CARLA\nlight state for six brake/reverse steps, with rear-camera frames.\n\nASPICE SWE.1-SWE.6 demonstration work products under az3166/aspice:\n- Requirements (6 SYS, 26 SWR) in Markdown\n- PlantUML architecture and detailed-design views, coding guidelines\n  with justified deviations\n- Unit, integration and qualification test specifications\n- generate_report.py: renders diagrams with a pinned PlantUML jar, runs\n  unit tests with gcov, cppcheck, MISRA baseline and lizard, checks\n  firmware identity/size/ThreadX pin, computes bidirectional\n  traceability and writes a self-contained HTML report\n\nNew SLCAN boundary unit test brings host-unit branch coverage to 100%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
